export default {"P001005":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Topological spaces · predicate · <code>P001005</code></p><h3>Admits a dimension function</h3><p>There exists an integer-valued dimension function on the space.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02IA\">Stacks 02IA · numbered source statement</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/topology/#tag-02IA\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001005\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001090":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Functors between specified covering-family sites · predicate · <code>P001090</code></p><h3>Almost cocontinuous functor</h3><p>For every target cover of u(U), a source cover of U exists such that on each member either its image is sheaf-theoretically empty or its map factors through some member of the given target cover.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04B7\">Stacks 04B7 · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 04B7 · per-member disjunction in the covering test</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-04B7\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001090\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001015":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Closed subschemes of locally Noetherian schemes · predicate · <code>P001015</code></p><h3>Ambient regularity along the divisor</h3><p>Fix a locally Noetherian scheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and a closed subscheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D\\subseteq X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. Each <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal O_{X,p}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> for <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p\\in D</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is regular. The condition only refers to points on <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BI9\">Stacks 0BI9 · numbered source and proof · Stacks 0BI9 · common source definition · Stacks 0BI9 · (regular local ambient rings at points on D)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/etale/#tag-0BI9\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001015\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001068":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Covariant functors from a small site to sets · predicate · <code>P001068</code></p><h3>Base-change bijections on covering arrows</h3><p>The comparison function from the value at any base change of a member of a cover to the fibre product of the values is a bijection.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Y5\">Stacks 00Y5 · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00Y5 · common source definition · Stacks 00Y5 · (2)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00Y5\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001068\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001035":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Small categories with a specified set of indexed families · predicate · <code>P001035</code></p><h3>Base-change stability of cover families</h3><p>For every cover and base change for which the indicated pullbacks exist, their family is a cover.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00VH\">Stacks 00VH · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00VH · common source definition · Stacks 00VH · (3) basechange</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00VH\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001035\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001030":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Morphisms of set-valued presheaves on a small category · predicate · <code>P001030</code></p><h3>Categorical epimorphism in presheaves</h3><p>The given presheaf map is a epimorphism in the presheaf category.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00V7\">Stacks 00V7 · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00V7\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001030\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001053":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Morphisms of set-valued sheaves on a site · predicate · <code>P001053</code></p><h3>Categorical epimorphism in sheaves on a site</h3><p>The given map is a epimorphism in the category of sheaves.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00WN\">Stacks 00WN · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00WN\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001053\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001031":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Morphisms of set-valued presheaves on a small category · predicate · <code>P001031</code></p><h3>Categorical isomorphism in presheaves</h3><p>The given presheaf map is a isomorphism in the presheaf category.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00V7\">Stacks 00V7 · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00V7\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001031\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001054":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Morphisms of set-valued sheaves on a site · predicate · <code>P001054</code></p><h3>Categorical isomorphism in sheaves on a site</h3><p>The given map is a isomorphism in the category of sheaves.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00WN\">Stacks 00WN · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00WN\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001054\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001029":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Morphisms of set-valued presheaves on a small category · predicate · <code>P001029</code></p><h3>Categorical monomorphism in presheaves</h3><p>The given presheaf map is a monomorphism in the presheaf category.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00V7\">Stacks 00V7 · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00V7\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001029\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001052":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Morphisms of set-valued sheaves on a site · predicate · <code>P001052</code></p><h3>Categorical monomorphism in sheaves on a site</h3><p>The given map is a monomorphism in the category of sheaves.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00WN\">Stacks 00WN · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00WN\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001052\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001092":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Geometric morphisms between Grothendieck topoi · predicate · <code>P001092</code></p><h3>Closed immersion of topoi</h3><p>A geometric embedding whose direct-image essential image is a closed subtopos.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08M0\">Stacks 08M0 · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 08M0 · common source definition · Stacks 08M0 · (2)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-08M0\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001092\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001064":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Functors between specified covering-family sites · predicate · <code>P001064</code></p><h3>Cocontinuous functor of sites</h3><p>Every covering family of an image object admits a refinement by the image of a covering family of its source object. The image family need not itself be a specified cover.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00XJ\">Stacks 00XJ · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00XJ · refinement of covers of image objects</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00XJ\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001064\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001033":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Small categories with a specified set of indexed families · predicate · <code>P001033</code></p><h3>Composition of covers</h3><p>Given a cover of an object and a chosen cover of each source, the indexed composite family is in the specified set.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00VH\">Stacks 00VH · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00VH · common source definition · Stacks 00VH · (2)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00VH\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001033\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001055":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Functors between specified covering-family sites · predicate · <code>P001055</code></p><h3>Continuous functor between covering-family sites</h3><p>It sends every covering family to a covering family and preserves its base changes along every map into the covering target.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00WV\">Stacks 00WV · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00WV · common source definition · Stacks 00WV · continuous functor</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00WV\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001055\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001045":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Covariant functors from a small site to sets · predicate · <code>P001045</code></p><h3>Covering-sieve surjectivity at a functor</h3><p>For each covering sieve the inclusion into the corresponding representable induces a surjection on the stalks defined by the chosen functor.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00ZT\">Stacks 00ZT · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00ZT · common source definition · Stacks 00ZT · (1)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00ZT\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001045\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001002":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Topological spaces with an integer-valued function · predicate · <code>P001002</code></p><h3>Dimension function</h3><p>The designated integer function strictly decreases under every specialization of distinct points and decreases by exactly one under immediate specialization.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02I9\">Stacks 02I9 · numbered source statement · Stacks 02I9 · common source definition · Stacks 02I9 · (2)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/topology/#tag-02I9\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001002\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001071":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Geometric points of Grothendieck topoi · predicate · <code>P001071</code></p><h3>Direct image of the point preserves all small limits</h3><p>Its direct image sends each limiting cone of sets to a limiting cone in its target topos.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05UY\">Stacks 05UY · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-05UY\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001071\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001070":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Geometric points of Grothendieck topoi · predicate · <code>P001070</code></p><h3>Direct image of the point preserves every coequalizer</h3><p>For each parallel pair of functions, the image of its coequalizer under the specified point direct image must be a coequalizer in the topos.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05UY\">Stacks 05UY · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-05UY\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001070\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001014":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Closed subschemes of locally Noetherian schemes · predicate · <code>P001014</code></p><h3>Effective Cartier divisor on a locally Noetherian ambient scheme</h3><p>Fix a locally Noetherian scheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and a closed subscheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D\\subseteq X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. The ideal of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is locally generated by one nonzerodivisor.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BI9\">Stacks 0BI9 · numbered source and proof · Stacks 0BI9 · common source definition · Stacks 0BI9 · (effective Cartier condition)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/etale/#tag-0BI9\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BSF\">Stacks 0BSF · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/etale/#tag-0BSF\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001014\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001020":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Closed subschemes of locally Noetherian schemes · predicate · <code>P001020</code></p><h3>Effective Cartier irreducible components</h3><p>Fix a locally Noetherian scheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and a closed subscheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D\\subseteq X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. Every irreducible component of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> with its reduced induced structure is an effective Cartier divisor on <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BIA\">Stacks 0BIA · numbered source and proof · Stacks 0BIA · (2) component Cartier condition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/etale/#tag-0BIA\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001020\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001089":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Objects of a specified site · predicate · <code>P001089</code></p><h3>Empty covering family</h3><p>The empty family is a covering of the specified object.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04B6\">Stacks 04B6 · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-04B6\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001089\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001076":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Geometric morphisms between Grothendieck topoi · predicate · <code>P001076</code></p><h3>Epimorphic counit</h3><p>The counit from inverse image after direct image is epic on every sheaf.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04D6\">Stacks 04D6 · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-04D6\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001076\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001016":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Closed subschemes of locally Noetherian schemes · predicate · <code>P001016</code></p><h3>Equation given by distinct regular parameters</h3><p>Fix a locally Noetherian scheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and a closed subscheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D\\subseteq X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. At every <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> the local ideal is generated by a product of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r\\ge1</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> different members of a regular system of parameters in the regular local ambient ring at <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BI9\">Stacks 0BI9 · numbered source and proof · Stacks 0BI9 · common source definition · Stacks 0BI9 · (local parameter equation)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/etale/#tag-0BI9\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001016\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001009":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Ring homomorphisms · predicate · <code>P001009</code></p><h3>Étale local homomorphism in the Noetherian convention</h3><p>Let <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A\\to B</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> be a local homomorphism of Noetherian local rings. The map is flat and unramified in the local-ring sense of Tag 024M.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0258\">Stacks 0258 · numbered source and proof · Stacks 0258 · common source definition · Stacks 0258 · étale local homomorphism</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/etale/#tag-0258\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://www.iut-theory.org/divers/ega44.pdf\">Grothendieck–Dieudonné, EGA IV₄, 17.6.1 and 17.6.3, local and completed étale criteria</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001009\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001024":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Closed subschemes of locally Noetherian schemes · predicate · <code>P001024</code></p><h3>Étale-local strict normal crossings models</h3><p>Fix a locally Noetherian scheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and a closed subscheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D\\subseteq X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. For each point of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, an étale map from a scheme with that point in its image pulls <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> back to a strict normal crossings divisor.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BSF\">Stacks 0BSF · numbered source and proof · Stacks 0BSF · common source definition · Stacks 0BSF · existence of étale-local strict models</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/etale/#tag-0BSF\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001024\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001073":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Objects of a specified site · predicate · <code>P001073</code></p><h3>Evaluation at a site object preserves surjections</h3><p>Every surjection of sheaves of sets induces a surjection upon evaluation at this object.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/090K\">Stacks 090K · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-090K\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001073\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001011":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Morphisms of schemes · predicate · <code>P001011</code></p><h3>Every fibre is empty or the residue-field point</h3><p>For every target point <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, the fibre is empty or its structure morphism to <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Spec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Spec}\\kappa(s)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is an isomorphism.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05VH\">Stacks 05VH · numbered source and proof · Stacks 05VH · (5) fibre condition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/etale/#tag-05VH\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001011\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001046":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Covariant functors from a small site to sets · predicate · <code>P001046</code></p><h3>Exactness of the stalk on sheaves</h3><p>The stalk defined by the chosen functor preserves finite limits and finite colimits on sheaves.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00ZT\">Stacks 00ZT · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00ZT · common source definition · Stacks 00ZT · (2)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00ZT\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001046\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001088":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Objects of a specified site · predicate · <code>P001088</code></p><h3>Existence of an initial-sheaf section</h3><p>The initial sheaf has at least one section on the object.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04B6\">Stacks 04B6 · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-04B6\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001088\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001034":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Small categories with a specified set of indexed families · predicate · <code>P001034</code></p><h3>Existence of pullbacks of covering arrows</h3><p>Each arrow of a covering family has a fibre product along every arrow into its target.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00VH\">Stacks 00VH · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00VH · common source definition · Stacks 00VH · (3) pullbacks</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00VH\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001034\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001022":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Closed subschemes of locally Noetherian schemes · predicate · <code>P001022</code></p><h3>Expected codimension for intersections of components</h3><p>Fix a locally Noetherian scheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and a closed subscheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D\\subseteq X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. For each nonempty finite set of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> distinct reduced components, every irreducible component of their scheme-theoretic intersection has codimension <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> in <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BIA\">Stacks 0BIA · numbered source and proof · Stacks 0BIA · (2) expected codimension</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/etale/#tag-0BIA\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001022\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001074":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Geometric morphisms between Grothendieck topoi · predicate · <code>P001074</code></p><h3>Faithful direct image</h3><p>Direct image is faithful.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04D6\">Stacks 04D6 · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-04D6\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001074\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001061":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Objects of a specified site · predicate · <code>P001061</code></p><h3>Finite covering subfamily of every cover</h3><p>Every covering family has a finite subfamily belonging to the specified covering presentation.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D05\">Stacks 0D05 · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-0D05\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001061\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001060":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Objects of a specified site · predicate · <code>P001060</code></p><h3>Finite refinement of every cover</h3><p>Every cover of the object admits a finite covering family refining it.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D05\">Stacks 0D05 · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-0D05\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001060\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001047":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Pairs of indexed families with a common target · predicate · <code>P001047</code></p><h3>First indexed family refines the second</h3><p>Over a fixed common target there is a family morphism whose target component is the identity.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00VT\">Stacks 00VT · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00VT · common source definition · Stacks 00VT · (2)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00VT\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001047\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001040":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Ordered pairs of topologies on one small category · predicate · <code>P001040</code></p><h3>First topology finer than the second</h3><p>For a pair (J,K) on one category, every K-covering sieve is J-covering. Equivalently K is coarser than J.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Z6\">Stacks 00Z6 · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00Z6 · order and its opposite terminology</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00Z6\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001040\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001013":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Morphisms of schemes · predicate · <code>P001013</code></p><h3>Formally étale morphism of schemes</h3><p>For every affine scheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> over the target and every square-zero closed subscheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_0</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, restriction gives a bijection on maps from <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_0</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> over the target.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/025K\">Stacks 025K · numbered source and proof · Stacks 025K · (2) bijectivity of restriction</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/etale/#tag-025K\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001013\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001010":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Morphisms of schemes · predicate · <code>P001010</code></p><h3>Formally unramified morphism of schemes</h3><p>For every affine scheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> over the target and square-zero closed immersion <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>↪</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_0\\hookrightarrow T</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, restriction of target-relative maps to the source is injective.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/024R\">Stacks 024R · numbered source and proof · Stacks 024R · (2) uniqueness of lifts</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/etale/#tag-024R\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001010\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001075":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Geometric morphisms between Grothendieck topoi · predicate · <code>P001075</code></p><h3>Fully faithful direct image</h3><p>Direct image is fully faithful.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04D6\">Stacks 04D6 · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-04D6\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08LU\">Stacks 08LU · embedding iff the direct image is fully faithful</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-08LU\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001075\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001058":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Functors between specified covering-family sites · predicate · <code>P001058</code></p><h3>Functor defining a morphism of sites in the opposite direction</h3><p>The functor is continuous and its sheafified left Kan extension is exact. As a left adjoint this extension preserves all small colimits, so finite-limit preservation is the extra requirement.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00X1\">Stacks 00X1 · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00X1 · morphism of sites</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00X1\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001058\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001000":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Continuous maps of topological spaces · predicate · <code>P001000</code></p><h3>Generalizing continuous map</h3><p>For any source point, each generalization of its image lifts to a generalization of that original point.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0063\">Stacks 0063 · numbered source statement · Stacks 0063 · common source definition · Stacks 0063 · (2)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/topology/#tag-0063\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001000\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001099":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Spaces with a specified family of subsets · predicate · <code>P001099</code></p><h3>Good stratification</h3><p>A locally closed partition such that whenever a part meets the closure of another part it is contained in that closure.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09Y0\">Stacks 09Y0 · numbered source statement · Stacks 09Y0 · frontier condition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/topology/#tag-09Y0\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001099\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001001":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Spaces with two ordered points · predicate · <code>P001001</code></p><h3>Immediate specialization</h3><p>The points are distinct, the first specializes to the second, and no third point lies between them in the specialization preorder.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02I9\">Stacks 02I9 · numbered source statement · Stacks 02I9 · common source definition · Stacks 02I9 · (1)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/topology/#tag-02I9\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001001\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001050":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Morphisms of set-valued sheaves on a site · predicate · <code>P001050</code></p><h3>Injective map of sheaves on a site</h3><p>Its map on sections at each object is injective.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00WM\">Stacks 00WM · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00WM · common source definition · Stacks 00WM · (1)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00WM\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001050\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001080":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Geometric morphisms between Grothendieck topoi · predicate · <code>P001080</code></p><h3>Invertible counit</h3><p>The geometric adjunction counit is an isomorphism on every object of the source topos.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04D6\">Stacks 04D6 · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-04D6\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001080\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001095":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Continuous maps of topological spaces · predicate · <code>P001095</code></p><h3>Irreducible surjection of spaces</h3><p>The map is surjective and no proper closed subset of its domain maps onto its codomain.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08YJ\">Stacks 08YJ · numbered source statement</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/topology/#tag-08YJ\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001095\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001096":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Topological spaces with a specified point · predicate · <code>P001096</code></p><h3>Isolated point</h3><p>The singleton of the designated point is open.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06RM\">Stacks 06RM · numbered source statement · Stacks 06RM · open singleton</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/topology/#tag-06RM\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001096\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001032":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Small categories with a specified set of indexed families · predicate · <code>P001032</code></p><h3>Isomorphism covers</h3><p>Every isomorphism, taken as a singleton family, belongs to the specified set of covering families.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00VH\">Stacks 00VH · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00VH · common source definition · Stacks 00VH · (1)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00VH\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001032\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001067":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Covariant functors from a small site to sets · predicate · <code>P001067</code></p><h3>Joint surjectivity on covering families</h3><p>The coproduct of the values on the source objects of each cover maps onto the value on its target.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Y5\">Stacks 00Y5 · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00Y5 · common source definition · Stacks 00Y5 · (1)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00Y5\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001067\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001069":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Covariant functors from a small site to sets · predicate · <code>P001069</code></p><h3>Left exactness of the stalk on sheaves</h3><p>Taking the stalk defined by the functor preserves finite limits of sheaves.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Y5\">Stacks 00Y5 · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00Y5 · common source definition · Stacks 00Y5 · (3)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00Y5\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001069\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001038":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Small categories with a specified assignment of sieves · predicate · <code>P001038</code></p><h3>Local character of covering sieves</h3><p>If a sieve pulls back to a covering sieve along every arrow of one covering sieve on the same target, then it covers.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Z4\">Stacks 00Z4 · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00Z4 · common source definition · Stacks 00Z4 · (2)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00Z4\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://fabrice.orgogozo.perso.math.cnrs.fr/SGA4/originaux/SGA4-IIo.pdf\">SGA 4, Exposé II, Définition 1.1</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001038\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001039":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Small categories with a specified assignment of sieves · predicate · <code>P001039</code></p><h3>Maximal sieves cover</h3><p>The maximal sieve on each object is covering.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Z4\">Stacks 00Z4 · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00Z4 · common source definition · Stacks 00Z4 · (3)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00Z4\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://fabrice.orgogozo.perso.math.cnrs.fr/SGA4/originaux/SGA4-IIo.pdf\">SGA 4, Exposé II, Définition 1.1</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001039\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001048":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Pairs of indexed families with a common target · predicate · <code>P001048</code></p><h3>Mutual refinement of indexed families</h3><p>Each of the two families refines the other over the identity of their common target.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00VV\">Stacks 00VV · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00VV\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001048\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001023":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Closed subschemes of locally Noetherian schemes · predicate · <code>P001023</code></p><h3>Normal crossings divisor</h3><p>Fix a locally Noetherian scheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and a closed subscheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D\\subseteq X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. An effective Cartier divisor such that every point of its support is in the image of an étale <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U\\to X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> for which the entire pullback is a strict normal crossings divisor on <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BSF\">Stacks 0BSF · numbered source and proof · Stacks 0BSF · common source definition · Stacks 0BSF · normal crossings divisor</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/etale/#tag-0BSF\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001023\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001093":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Topological spaces with a specified subset · predicate · <code>P001093</code></p><h3>Nowhere dense subset</h3><p>The closure of the designated subset has empty interior.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03HN\">Stacks 03HN · numbered source statement · Stacks 03HN · common source definition · Stacks 03HN · (2)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/topology/#tag-03HN\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001093\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001027":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Morphisms of set-valued presheaves on a small category · predicate · <code>P001027</code></p><h3>Objectwise injective morphism of presheaves</h3><p>The function on sections at every object is injective.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00V6\">Stacks 00V6 · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00V6 · common source definition · Stacks 00V6 · (1)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00V6\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001027\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001028":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Morphisms of set-valued presheaves on a small category · predicate · <code>P001028</code></p><h3>Objectwise surjective morphism of presheaves</h3><p>The function on sections at every object is surjective.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00V6\">Stacks 00V6 · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00V6 · common source definition · Stacks 00V6 · (2)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00V6\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001028\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001091":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Geometric morphisms between Grothendieck topoi · predicate · <code>P001091</code></p><h3>Open immersion of topoi</h3><p>A geometric embedding whose direct-image essential image is an open subtopos.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08M0\">Stacks 08M0 · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 08M0 · common source definition · Stacks 08M0 · (1)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-08M0\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001091\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001097":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Spaces with a specified family of subsets · predicate · <code>P001097</code></p><h3>Partition into locally closed parts</h3><p>The indexed subsets are locally closed, pairwise disjoint, and cover the ambient space.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09XZ\">Stacks 09XZ · numbered source statement · Stacks 09XZ · common source definition · Stacks 09XZ · partition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/topology/#tag-09XZ\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001097\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001094":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Topological spaces with a specified subset · predicate · <code>P001094</code></p><h3>Patch-closed subset of a spectral space</h3><p>The ambient space is spectral and the given subset is closed in its constructible topology.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0902\">Stacks 0902 · numbered source statement</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/topology/#tag-0902\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001094\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001066":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Covariant functors from a small site to sets · predicate · <code>P001066</code></p><h3>Point of a covering-family site</h3><p>A covariant functor to sets carrying covering families to jointly surjective families, preserving base changes of covering arrows, and whose stalk on sheaves preserves finite limits.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Y5\">Stacks 00Y5 · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00Y5 · common source definition · Stacks 00Y5 · site point</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00Y5\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001066\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001044":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Covariant functors from a small site to sets · predicate · <code>P001044</code></p><h3>Point of a topology in sieves</h3><p>For the chosen covariant set functor u, the stalk is the colimit of presheaf sections over the opposite of its category of elements. It must be exact on sheaves and take every covering-sieve inclusion into its representable to a surjection.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00ZT\">Stacks 00ZT · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00ZT · common source definition · Stacks 00ZT · point of the topology</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00ZT\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001044\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001078":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Geometric morphisms between Grothendieck topoi · predicate · <code>P001078</code></p><h3>Preservation of coequalizers by direct image</h3><p>Direct image preserves all coequalizers of pairs of sheaf maps.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04D6\">Stacks 04D6 · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-04D6\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001078\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001057":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Functors between specified covering-family sites · predicate · <code>P001057</code></p><h3>Preservation of pullbacks of covering arrows</h3><p>For every member of a source covering and arrow to its target the comparison with the target pullback exists and is invertible.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00WV\">Stacks 00WV · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00WV · common source definition · Stacks 00WV · (2)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00WV\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001057\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001079":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Geometric morphisms between Grothendieck topoi · predicate · <code>P001079</code></p><h3>Preservation of pushouts by direct image</h3><p>Direct image preserves all pushouts of sheaves.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04D6\">Stacks 04D6 · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-04D6\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001079\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001077":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Geometric morphisms between Grothendieck topoi · predicate · <code>P001077</code></p><h3>Preservation of surjections by direct image</h3><p>Direct image takes every epimorphism of sheaves to an epimorphism.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04D6\">Stacks 04D6 · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-04D6\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001077\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001056":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Functors between specified covering-family sites · predicate · <code>P001056</code></p><h3>Preservation of the specified covering families</h3><p>The indexed image of every source covering is a target covering.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00WV\">Stacks 00WV · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00WV · common source definition · Stacks 00WV · (1)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00WV\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001056\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001059":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Objects of a specified site · predicate · <code>P001059</code></p><h3>Quasi-compact object of a site</h3><p>Each covering has a covering refinement whose map of index sets has finite image in the original indexing set.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/090H\">Stacks 090H · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 090H · finite-image refinement</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-090H\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001059\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001062":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Objects of a specified topos · predicate · <code>P001062</code></p><h3>Quasi-compact object of a topos</h3><p>For every epimorphism from a coproduct to the specified object, a finite subcoproduct still maps epimorphically onto it.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D07\">Stacks 0D07 · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 0D07 · common source definition · Stacks 0D07 · quasi-compact object</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-0D07\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001062\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001063":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Grothendieck topoi · predicate · <code>P001063</code></p><h3>Quasi-compact topos</h3><p>The terminal object of the topos is quasi-compact.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D07\">Stacks 0D07 · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 0D07 · common source definition · Stacks 0D07 · quasi-compact topos</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-0D07\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001063\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001012":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Morphisms of schemes · predicate · <code>P001012</code></p><h3>Quotient map on underlying Zariski spaces</h3><p>The map is surjective and a subset of its target is open exactly when its inverse image is open.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0256\">Stacks 0256 · numbered source and proof</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/etale/#tag-0256\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001012\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001019":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Closed subschemes of locally Noetherian schemes · predicate · <code>P001019</code></p><h3>Reduced closed subscheme</h3><p>Fix a locally Noetherian scheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and a closed subscheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D\\subseteq X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. The closed subscheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is reduced.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BIA\">Stacks 0BIA · numbered source and proof · Stacks 0BIA · (2) reducedness</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/etale/#tag-0BIA\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001019\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001098":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Spaces with an ordered pair of partitions · predicate · <code>P001098</code></p><h3>Refinement of a locally closed partition</h3><p>Each part of the coarser partition is the union of parts of the finer partition.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09XZ\">Stacks 09XZ · numbered source statement · Stacks 09XZ · common source definition · Stacks 09XZ · refinement relation</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/topology/#tag-09XZ\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001098\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001084":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Geometric morphisms between Grothendieck topoi · predicate · <code>P001084</code></p><h3>Refinement of surjections onto an inverse image</h3><p>For every epimorphism <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>→</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A\\to f^{-1}B</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> there is an epimorphism <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">′</mo></msup><mo>→</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B&#x27;\\to B</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> such that <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>B</mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">′</mo></msup><mo>→</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f^{-1}B&#x27;\\to f^{-1}B</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> factors through <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04D6\">Stacks 04D6 · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-04D6\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001084\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001081":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Geometric morphisms between Grothendieck topoi · predicate · <code>P001081</code></p><h3>Reflection of injections by direct image</h3><p>A sheaf map is monic whenever its direct image is monic.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04D6\">Stacks 04D6 · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-04D6\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001081\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001083":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Geometric morphisms between Grothendieck topoi · predicate · <code>P001083</code></p><h3>Reflection of isomorphisms by direct image</h3><p>A sheaf map is invertible whenever its direct image is invertible.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04D6\">Stacks 04D6 · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-04D6\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001083\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001082":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Geometric morphisms between Grothendieck topoi · predicate · <code>P001082</code></p><h3>Reflection of surjections by direct image</h3><p>A sheaf map is epic whenever its direct image is epic.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04D6\">Stacks 04D6 · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-04D6\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001082\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001018":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Closed subschemes of locally Noetherian schemes · predicate · <code>P001018</code></p><h3>Regular ambient scheme</h3><p>Fix a locally Noetherian scheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and a closed subscheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D\\subseteq X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. Every local ring of the ambient scheme is regular.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BIA\">Stacks 0BIA · numbered source and proof</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/etale/#tag-0BIA\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001018\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001021":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Closed subschemes of locally Noetherian schemes · predicate · <code>P001021</code></p><h3>Regular intersections of distinct components</h3><p>Fix a locally Noetherian scheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and a closed subscheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D\\subseteq X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. For each finite nonempty collection of distinct reduced components of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, their scheme-theoretic intersection in <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is regular.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BIA\">Stacks 0BIA · numbered source and proof · Stacks 0BIA · (2) regular intersections</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/etale/#tag-0BIA\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001021\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001043":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Ordered pairs of topologies on one small category · predicate · <code>P001043</code></p><h3>Reverse inclusion of sheaf subcategories</h3><p>For an ordered pair (J,K) on the same category, every J-sheaf is a K-sheaf in the common presheaf category.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00ZQ\">Stacks 00ZQ · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00ZQ\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001043\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001042":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Presheaves on a small category with specified topology when needed · predicate · <code>P001042</code></p><h3>Separated presheaf for a sieve topology</h3><p>For every covering sieve <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> on <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, restriction <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Hom</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(U)\\to\\operatorname{Hom}(S,F)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is injective.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00ZI\">Stacks 00ZI · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00ZI · separated for a sieve topology</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00ZI\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://fabrice.orgogozo.perso.math.cnrs.fr/SGA4/originaux/SGA4-IIo.pdf\">SGA 4, Exposé II, Définition 2.1</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001042\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001049":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Presheaves on a small category with specified topology when needed · predicate · <code>P001049</code></p><h3>Separated presheaf for covering families</h3><p>For each cover the map from sections on its target to the product of sections on its members is injective.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00WA\">Stacks 00WA · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00WA · joint injectivity</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00WA\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001049\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001036":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Presheaves on a small category with specified topology when needed · predicate · <code>P001036</code></p><h3>Sheaf condition for covering families</h3><p>For each cover <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>→</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(U_i\\to U)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, sections on <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> identify with tuples of sections on <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U_i</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> with equal restrictions to every <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mo>×</mo><mi>U</mi></msub><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U_i\\times_U U_j</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00VM\">Stacks 00VM · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00VM · equalizer condition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00VM\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001036\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001041":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Presheaves on a small category with specified topology when needed · predicate · <code>P001041</code></p><h3>Sheaf condition for covering sieves</h3><p>For every <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S\\in J(U)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> the map <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Hom</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Hom</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(U)=\\operatorname{Hom}(h_U,F)\\to\\operatorname{Hom}(S,F)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is bijective.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Z8\">Stacks 00Z8 · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00Z8 · sheaf for a sieve topology</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00Z8\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://fabrice.orgogozo.perso.math.cnrs.fr/SGA4/originaux/SGA4-IIo.pdf\">SGA 4, Exposé II, Définition 2.1</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001041\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001085":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Objects of a specified site · predicate · <code>P001085</code></p><h3>Sheaf-theoretically empty site object</h3><p>The natural map from the initial sheaf to the sheafified representable of the object is an isomorphism.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04B5\">Stacks 04B5 · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 04B5 · initiality of the associated representable</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-04B5\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001085\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001086":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Objects of a specified site · predicate · <code>P001086</code></p><h3>Singleton sections for every sheaf</h3><p>Every sheaf of sets has exactly one section on the object.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04B6\">Stacks 04B6 · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-04B6\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001086\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001087":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Objects of a specified site · predicate · <code>P001087</code></p><h3>Singleton sections of the initial sheaf</h3><p>The initial sheaf has exactly one section on the object.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04B6\">Stacks 04B6 · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-04B6\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001087\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001065":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Functors between specified covering-family sites · predicate · <code>P001065</code></p><h3>Special cocontinuous functor</h3><p>A continuous and cocontinuous functor which is locally faithful, locally full and covering-dense as in 03A0 and whose induced geometric morphism is an equivalence.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03CG\">Stacks 03CG · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 03CG · special cocontinuous functor</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-03CG\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001065\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001072":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Objects of a specified site · predicate · <code>P001072</code></p><h3>Splitting of every cover after sheafification</h3><p>For every cover of U the canonical map from the sheaf coproduct of the sheafified source representables to the sheafified target representable admits a section.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/090K\">Stacks 090K · numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-090K\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001072\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001037":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Small categories with a specified assignment of sieves · predicate · <code>P001037</code></p><h3>Stability of covering sieves under pullback</h3><p>Pulling a designated covering sieve back along any arrow gives a covering sieve.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Z4\">Stacks 00Z4 · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00Z4 · common source definition · Stacks 00Z4 · (1)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00Z4\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://fabrice.orgogozo.perso.math.cnrs.fr/SGA4/originaux/SGA4-IIo.pdf\">SGA 4, Exposé II, Définition 1.1</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001037\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001003":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Topological spaces with an integer-valued function · predicate · <code>P001003</code></p><h3>Strict decrease along specializations</h3><p>For every specialization between distinct points the function value strictly decreases.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02I9\">Stacks 02I9 · numbered source statement · Stacks 02I9 · common source definition · Stacks 02I9 · (2a)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/topology/#tag-02I9\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001003\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001017":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Closed subschemes of locally Noetherian schemes · predicate · <code>P001017</code></p><h3>Strict normal crossings divisor</h3><p>Fix a locally Noetherian scheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and a closed subscheme <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D\\subseteq X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. An effective Cartier divisor which, at every point of its support, is cut out in a regular local ring by a product of distinct members of one regular system of parameters.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BI9\">Stacks 0BI9 · numbered source and proof · Stacks 0BI9 · common source definition · Stacks 0BI9 · strict normal crossings divisor</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/etale/#tag-0BI9\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001017\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001051":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Morphisms of set-valued sheaves on a site · predicate · <code>P001051</code></p><h3>Surjective map of sheaves on a site</h3><p>Each target section becomes the image of a source section on every member of a suitable covering.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00WM\">Stacks 00WM · numbered Stacks Project source · Stacks 00WM · common source definition · Stacks 00WM · (2)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00WM\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001051\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001004":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Topological spaces with an integer-valued function · predicate · <code>P001004</code></p><h3>Unit drop on immediate specializations</h3><p>Along every immediate specialization the earlier value exceeds the later value by one.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02I9\">Stacks 02I9 · numbered source statement · Stacks 02I9 · common source definition · Stacks 02I9 · (2b)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/topology/#tag-02I9\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001004\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P001006":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Ring homomorphisms · predicate · <code>P001006</code></p><h3>Unramified local homomorphism in the Noetherian convention</h3><p>Let <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A\\to B</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> be a local homomorphism of Noetherian local rings. The target is essentially of finite type, its maximal ideal is generated by the source maximal ideal, and its residue extension is finite separable. This definition concerns local rings; the unlocalized algebra need not be of finite type.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/024M\">Stacks 024M · numbered source and proof · Stacks 024M · common source definition · Stacks 024M · definition with (1)–(3)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/etale/#tag-024M\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://www.iut-theory.org/divers/ega44.pdf\">Grothendieck–Dieudonné, EGA IV₄, 17.4.1 and 17.4.4, under the finite presentation or Noetherian hypotheses there</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0258\">Stacks 0258 · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/etale/#tag-0258\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#P001006\">Open shared record</a></p></article>"};
